\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.2}What the comparison contains decides the answer}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{res:panels}{{3.2}{11}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces What the comparison contains decides the answer. (a) For each agent, the distance to the nearest incumbent simulant (circles) and to the nearest candidate once the five further compounds treated as simulants in the literature are included (diamonds), as multiples of the typical nearest-neighbour separation of the merged space on the thirty-five-compound panel. A match requires a normalised distance below the dashed threshold \emph  {and} a distance smaller than that to every compound not designated a simulant, so sarin, soman and cyclosarin fail on the primary panel despite lying inside the threshold. (b) Matched agents under 1000 descriptor-resampling replicates (Supporting Information Section~\ref {S-meth:dboot}) for the incumbent three and for the eight literature-used simulants examined here; circles are means, vertical rules medians, bars the 2.5th to 97.5th percentiles across replicates. (c) On the twenty-eight-compound panel, which omits those five, the distance from each agent to its nearest incumbent simulant in each of the three spaces, normalised by the typical nearest-neighbour separation of that space; filled markers are valid matches. (d) Exact permutation null for that panel over all 680 ways of designating three of the seventeen non-agents as simulants, with the actual designation marked; the $p$ shown is the mean-difference statistic only, the other five and the adjusted values being in Supporting Information Table~\ref {S-tab:ablation}, where the Benjamini-Hochberg value over its eighteen tests is 0.163. (e) The same comparison on the volatility axis, which is one measured quantity rather than a descriptor set: for each agent the gap in $\log _{10}(P/\mathrm  {mmHg})$ to the nearest incumbent simulant and, where an interferent is nearer, to that compound. Three of the eleven agents are nearer an interferent here as well. The one pairing inside the match criterion, soman to DPGME, lies 0.0107 decades apart, between measurements made at different temperatures, and that separation is smaller than the mismatch (Supporting Information Section~\ref {S-meth:vol}).}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
